    "markdown": "# Knowledge Base: bezout-identity-oq-02-oq-01-oq-02-oq-02\n\n## Problem Understanding\n\nThe problem asks for a Lean gallery proof about Gaussian integers. The local notes state that \\(\\mathbb{Z}[i]\\) is a Euclidean domain with Euclidean function \\(N(a+bi)=a^2+b^2\\), and ask whether the gallery can formalize unique factorization in \\(\\mathbb{Z}[i]\\) together with a characterization of Gaussian primes.\n\n## Known Mathematical Target\n\nThe source notes include the classical integer-prime classification: a prime \\(p \\in \\mathbb{Z}\\) remains prime in \\(\\mathbb{Z}[i]\\) iff \\(p \\equiv 3 \\pmod 4\\); otherwise it splits as \\(p=\\pi\\overline{\\pi}\\).\n\n## Current Research State\n\nThe state file is still in OBSERVE phase on the fast path, with no active approach, no attempts, and no blockers. The next action is to do a quick Mathlib search and move to ACT if an obvious approach is found.\n\n## Next Steps\n\nCheck `Mathlib.NumberTheory.GaussianInt` for existing Gaussian integer infrastructure, identify gaps around Gaussian prime characterization and the UFD proof, and build on that infrastructure where available.\n"
